From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: map SM8150 encoder capture buffers bidirectionally

The downstream SM8150 driver maps every encoder dma-buf with
DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL.  The VPU5 firmware may read bookkeeping from a compressed
capture buffer before writing the encoded payload.  Mapping that queue only
DMA_FROM_DEVICE therefore leaves the IOMMU mapping without read permission.

Test16 mapped only the raw input queue bidirectionally.  Its trace reaches
START, queues four FTBs with bidirectional=0, then hard-resets immediately
after the first ETB.  Match the downstream DMA contract for the capture queue
as well.  This also lets vb2-dma-contig perform the matching bidirectional
cache maintenance on non-coherent memory.

Keep the change limited to IRIS1 so other Venus generations retain their
existing DMA directions.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index 541162a4f7b9..baaa32d5bbcd 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -2143,6 +2143,18 @@ static int m2m_queue_init(void *priv, struct vb2_queue *src_vq,
 	dst_vq->min_queued_buffers = 1;
 	dst_vq->dev = inst->core->dev;
 	dst_vq->lock = &inst->ctx_q_lock;
+	/*
+	 * Downstream SM8150 maps every encoder dma-buf bidirectionally.  The
+	 * VPU5 firmware may read capture-buffer bookkeeping before writing the
+	 * encoded payload, so a DMA_FROM_DEVICE-only IOMMU mapping can fault
+	 * as soon as the first ETB makes the firmware consume an FTB.
+	 */
+	if (IS_IRIS1(inst->core))
+		dst_vq->bidirectional = 1;
+	if (IS_IRIS1(inst->core))
+		dev_info(inst->core->dev,
+			 "venus-sm8150: encoder capture DMA bidirectional=%u\n",
+			 dst_vq->bidirectional);
 	return vb2_queue_init(dst_vq);
 }
 
